the Navy officer in charge of the u.s.  7th fleet was relieved of his duties  overnight after the latest deadly  collision involving a destroyer the  removal of Vice Admiral Joseph a coin  follows a string of incidents involving  US warships the USS John S McCain  collided Monday with a commercial tanker  the second deadly accident in three  months for the fleet ten sailors are  thought to have died in this mishap Ben  Tracy is in Beijing and following the  Navy shake up and good morning good  morning it has been an absolutely  horrible summer for the u.s. seventh  Fleet which is based in Japan they have  likely lost 17 of their sailors two of  their warships are extensively damaged  and now the commander of the entire  fleet has lost his job the damage was  significant this was not a small  collision just two months ago Vice  Admiral Joseph altcoin promised a  sweeping investigation following the USS  fitzgerald's deadly collision with a  merchant ship off the coast of Japan but  after the USS John S McCain crashed  earlier this week the Navy decided to  remove all coin from his post as head of  the seventh Fleet the mccain's collision  was the latest of four incidents  involving his ships in just the past  eight months  Vice Admiral Aucoin has led the seventh  Fleet since September 2015 and was set  to retire next month the divers were  able locate some remains in those sealed  compartments in a press conference  yesterday Pacific Fleet Commander  Admiral Scott Swift said the Navy is  looking at all possible causes for the  collision between the McCain in an oil  tanker Monday near Singapore including a  cyberattack on the ship's controls he  promised to get to the root cause of  these incidents in the Pacific when  tragedy like this is one too many  and while each of these four events is  unique they cannot be viewed in  isolation the Navy has not released the  names of the McCain's missing sailors  but at least three of them have been  identified by family members the  families of Logan Palmer and Kenneth  Smith think those expressing concern for  their missing sons and Meagan Partlow  said of her missing fiance Jacob Drake I  am slowly losing hope and it hurts to  know I might never  to walk down the aisle to see the love  of my life the Navy is now expanding the  search area in the hopes of finding some  of these 10 missing sailors still alive  meanwhile the Pacific Fleet is going to  conduct what they're calling a  deliberate reset of all of their ships  basically here they're gonna bring in  experts who will assess and train all of  the crews that's a story thank you very  much Ben Tracy reporting from Beijing
 

